      "text": "The given problem involves calculating the sum of squares of several pairs of consecutive even numbers and then finding the result of a specific mathematical operation. We start with the squares of the pairs:\n\n1. \\(19^2\\)\n2. \\(17^2\\)\n3. \\(15^2\\)\n4. \\(13^2\\)\n5. \\(11^2\\)\n6. \\(9^2\\)\n7. \\(7^2\\)\n8. \\(5^2\\)\n9. \\(3^2\\)\n10. \\(1^2\\)\n\nWe can calculate each square individually and then sum them up:\n\n\\[\n19^2 = 361\n\\]\n\\[\n17^2 = 289\n\\]\n\\[\n15^2 = 225\n\\]\n\\[\n13^2 = 169\n\\]\n\\[\n11^2 = 121\n\\]\n\\[\n9^2 = 81\n\\]\n\\[\n7^2 = 49\n\\]\n\\[\n5^2 = 25\n\\]\n\\[\n3^2 = 9\n\\]\n\\[\n1^2 = 1\n\\]\n\nNext, we sum these squared values:\n\n\\[\n361 + 289 + 225 + 169 + 121 + 81 + 49 + 25 + 9 + 1\n\\]\n\nWe can add these step-by-step:\n\n\\[\n361 + 289 = 650\n\\]\n\\[\n650 + 225 = 875\n\\]\n\\[\n875 + 169 = 1044\n\\]\n\\[\n1044 + 121 = 1165\n\\]\n\\[\n1165 + 81 = 1246\n\\]\n\\[\n1246 + 49 = 1295\n\\]\n\\[\n1295 + 25 = 1320\n\\]\n\\[\n1320 + 9 = 1329\n\\]\n\\[\n1329 + 1 = 1330\n\\]\n\nThus, the sum of the squares is 1330.\n\nNow, the problem asks for the value of \\(19^2 - 17^2 + 15^2 - 13^2 + 11^2 - 9^2 + 7^2 - 5^2 + 3^2 - 1^2\\). We can rewrite this expression as:\n\n\\[\n19^2 - 17^2 + 15^2 - 13^2 + 11^2 - 9^2 + 7^2 - 5^2 + 3^2 - 1^2\n\\]\n\nThis can be expressed as:\n\n\\[\n(19^2 - 17^2) + (15^2 - 13^2) + (11^2 - 9^2) + (7^2 - 5^2) + (3^2 - 1^2)\n\\]\n\nWe can use the difference of squares formula, \\(a^2 - b^2 = (a - b)(a + b)\\) for each pair:\n\n\\[\n19^2 - 17^2 = (19 - 17)(19 + 17) = 2 \\cdot 36 = 72\n\\]\n\\[\n15^2 - 13^2 = (15 - 13)(15 + 13) = 2 \\cdot 28 = 56\n\\]\n\\[\n11^2 - 9^2 = (11 - 9)(11 + 9) = 2 \\cdot 20 = 40\n\\]\n\\[\n7^2 - 5^2 = (7 - 5)(7 + 5) = 2 \\cdot 12 = 24\n\\]\n\\[\n3^2 - 1^2 = (3 - 1)(3 + 1) = 2 \\cdot 4 = 8\n\\]\n\nAdding these results together:\n\n\\[\n72 + 56 + 40 + 24 + 8 = 200\n\\]\n\nThus, the value of the original expression is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{200}\n\\]",
