      "text": "The problem involves the application of the difference of squares formula, which states that \\(a^2 - b^2 = (a - b)(a + b)\\). We can apply this formula to each pair of terms in the given expression.\n\nLet's start by applying the difference of squares formula to each pair of terms:\n\n1. \\(19^2 - 17^2 = (19 - 17)(19 + 17) = 2 \\cdot 36 = 72\\)\n2. \\(15^2 - 13^2 = (15 - 13)(15 + 13) = 2 \\cdot 28 = 56\\)\n3. \\(11^2 - 9^2 = (11 - 9)(11 + 9) = 2 \\cdot 20 = 40\\)\n4. \\(9^2 - 7^2 = (9 - 7)(9 + 7) = 2 \\cdot 16 = 32\\)\n5. \\(7^2 - 5^2 = (7 - 5)(7 + 5) = 2 \\cdot 12 = 24\\)\n6. \\(5^2 - 3^2 = (5 - 3)(5 + 3) = 2 \\cdot 8 = 16\\)\n7. \\(3^2 - 1^2 = (3 - 1)(3 + 1) = 2 \\cdot 4 = 8\\)\n\nNow, we sum all these results:\n\n\\[72 + 56 + 40 + 32 + 24 + 16 + 8 = 240\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of the given expression is \\(\\boxed{240}\\).",
